 ## Changelog
+- `done` legacy frame: terrain lit in one forward pass; black-terrain flicker (written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain or a GPU: not compiled, not run; +1 test `gpu::pipeline::tests::chunk_shader_validates_and_legacy_is_forward` not run; numbers are from the OPPO A5i video `Record_2026-10-12-14-58-18.mp4`: 633 frames in 26.2 s, 41 ms average, 11 frames over 100 ms, FPS counter 16..43):
+    - Symptom, measured on the video: in ~85 of 633 frames most of the TERRAIN is black while the sky and the HUD are right; 2 frames are black through the whole scene area. Several of them show a lit screen-aligned rectangle (a block of tiles) inside the black, which is how a GPU tile that was not flushed / finished before it was read looks, not a NaN (a NaN in the post chain would blacken the sky too: the post chain was ruled out).
+    - Cause (UNVERIFIED on a device: it is the only pass pair in the legacy frame where a full-screen pass reads what an earlier pass just wrote): `fs_main` wrote albedo + a packed light value into an RGBA16F G-buffer, `copy_depth` copied the depth, and `fs_deferred` (full screen) read both back. Where its read raced the tile writes, the G-buffer reads as 0 = black albedo (cleared to transparent) under a depth that says "terrain".
+    - Fix: in legacy `fs_main` lights and fogs the texel itself (`photon_light` legacy branch, face 6, then `apply_fog`: the same maths `fs_deferred` did, so the picture does not change) and `lib.rs` draws terrain, items and outline straight into the scene pass (`draw_opaque`), then the sky (LessEqual: only the pixels still at depth 1), then water. Gone from the legacy frame: the G-buffer pass, `copy_depth`, the full-screen deferred pass, and the shaft march's first frame. The Photon look (`LEGACY = false`) keeps its G-buffer path unchanged.
+    - Cost: also one full-resolution RGBA16F write + read, one depth copy and one full-screen shading pass fewer per frame. `post.rs`: with `Settings.taa` off the TAA pass only copied the scene, so it is skipped (`draw`) and the bloom / grade read the scene directly (`targets`: `frame`).
+    - Not touched, and the likely next cost on a phone: chunk generation, populate, light and meshing run on the render thread (see Performance notes); the FPS log line's CPU ms/frame says whether a run is CPU-bound. Levers: `RENDER_SCALE`, `RENDER_DIST`, `AUTOSAVE_CHUNKS`, the 10 ms light budget in `world/chunks.rs`.
+    - ponytail: `Photon.gbuf` is still allocated in legacy (4 MB at 0.67 scale, unused); delete it with the Photon path when that goes.
 - `done` shader pass for the OPPO A5i video (black terrain flicker, dark leaves, no light shafts, ~6 fps). Written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain or a GPU: not compiled, not run; +1 test (`photon::deferred_shader_validates`), `vl` tests changed (`march_is_shafts_only_and_hdr` replaces `lookups_use_photons_shadow_code`). Numbers below are from the video (143 frames in 22.9 s: 160 ms average, 470 ms worst), not from a profiler:
     - Black flicker, root cause in `render/post.wgsl` TAA: `sqrt(m1 - m0 * m0)` (variance clip) rounds to a hair below 0 on flat areas -> NaN, which the old `max0v(history)` did not clear on every driver (it came back one frame later: the strobe). Also `reinhard_inverse` divided by `1 - x` with x >= 1 after the YCoCg clip, and CAS divided 0 / 0 on a black 3x3. Now `sane()` (integer test for the all-ones exponent, survives fast-math) guards the TAA inputs, history and output and the grade input, the variance is `max(.., 0)`, the inverse is clamped to < 1, CAS divides by `max(max_color, 1e-4)`. The deferred pass guards its own decode and output the same way.
     - Dark, flickering leaves: the surface shadow was computed in `vl.rs` at half resolution from a face normal rebuilt from the depth buffer; alpha-cut leaves have noisy depth, so the axis snap picked a wrong face and `n.L <= 0` shadowed them (the TAA jitter made it flicker). Now `photon.rs` `fs_deferred` looks the shadow up at full resolution with the G-buffer's exact face: normal offset of ~1.2 texels (x the distortion factor, more at grazing angles), a 0.15 block depth bias, 4 hardware-bilinear compares rotated by IGN, faded to `get_lightmap_shadows` at the map edge. Deleted from the march: `face_normal`, `view_pos`, the PCSS include and its blocker search (the `shadows::pcss_wgsl` code stays, unused). `Photon::new` / `draw_deferred` take the shadow group.
